<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 22 February, from 1495 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1495</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles VIII of France enters Naples</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a rapid march through Italy, the French king took Naples almost without a fight. A coalition of Italian states, Spain and the Emperor soon forced him out, but the Italian Wars had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1732</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington is born in Virginia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Born at Popes Creek in Westmoreland County, Washington commanded the Continental Army in the Revolutionary War and became the first President of the United States.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1819</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spain cedes Florida in the Adams-Onís Treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Spain gave Florida to the United States and agreed a boundary running to the Pacific. In return the US assumed claims of its citizens against Spain and gave up its claim to Texas.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1847</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Buena Vista begins in northern Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Zachary Taylor's outnumbered army held off Santa Anna's attacks over two days near Saltillo. Santa Anna withdrew, and Taylor's fame carried him to the presidency in 1848.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1980</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US amateurs beat the Soviet Union in the 'Miracle on Ice'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A team of American college players defeated the Soviet Union, four-time Olympic champions, 4-3 at the Lake Placid Winter Olympics. The US went on to win the gold medal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1997</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scientists announce Dolly the sheep, the first clone of an adult mammal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Researchers at the Roslin Institute near Edinburgh revealed they had cloned a sheep from an adult cell. Dolly, born in July 1996, sparked worldwide debate on the ethics of cloning.</p></li></ol>
